# WERDU.DE - PROJECT CONTEXT & INSTRUCTIONS

## 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW & ARCHITECTURE
- Website Domain: https://werdu.de (Production) / https://test.werdu.de (Staging)
- Environment: WordPress environment located in `/httpdocs`.
- Primary Business Model: Direct-to-consumer sales of home battery storage systems (Heimspeicher / LiFePO4 batteries) in Germany. Transparent pricing is available directly on the site.
- Primary Goal: Achieve #1 Rankings, top conversion rates, and dominate AI Search (AIO / GEO - ChatGPT Search, Perplexity, Google SGE/AIO) for home energy storage in Germany (2026).

## 2. AGENTIC CRO & LIGHT THEME DESIGN (FULL AUTHORITY)
Cursor has full authority to refactor UI, HTML, CSS, layout, and German copy for higher conversions (CRO) and modern aesthetics, provided the factual, URL, and hook rules in this file are kept.

Light theme is mandatory. Never ship dark-on-dark or dark marketing themes.

Design tokens (strict):
- Page background: white / light-grey `#f8fafc`
- Body text: dark blue `#0f172a`
- Muted text: `#475569`
- Borders: `#e2e8f0`
- Primary CTA: orange `#ff6600` (hover `#e05500`), white label text
- Cards: white `#ffffff` on the light page background

CTA buttons must be high-contrast orange on the light canvas. Product grids must keep equal card heights with CTAs aligned on one baseline.

## 3. ABSOLUTE TRUTH & FACT CHECKING
- NEVER invent facts, battery specs, prices, guarantee terms, funding amounts, or company attributes.
- ALWAYS verify German energy standards, LiFePO4 specifications, and tax rules before writing them.
- § 12 Abs. 3 UStG: 0 % MwSt on eligible PV systems and associated storage for residential / qualifying buildings. Do not invent extra tax exceptions.
- LiFePO4: use only established ranges already used on the site (typically 6.000–8.000 cycles and 15–20 years; product-specific values only when they already exist in WooCommerce / Preis-Manager data).
- Local installer option: optional shipping to a certified local installer. Do not invent a fixed setup fee; each mechanic sets their own hourly rates.
- Everything written MUST be 100 % accurate, EEAT-grade, and professional German.

## 4. ZERO BROKEN LINKS
- NEVER construct hallucinated or non-existent URLs.
- ONLY link internally to validated sitemap URLs in Section 8 (e.g. `/solarbatterie-rechner/`, `/shop/`, `/beratung-anfragen/`).
- External references must point exclusively to genuine authority portals (e.g. Bundesnetzagentur, Verbraucherzentrale, Fraunhofer ISE) using `target="_blank" rel="noopener"`.

## 5. CALCULATORS & LEAD FLOW ARCHITECTURE
We have 3 Calculators on the site:
1. Calculator 1 (Main/Detailed): https://werdu.de/solarbatterie-rechner/
2. Calculator 2 (Homepage Preview/Quick): https://werdu.de/
3. Calculator 3 (Gratis Online Rechner): https://werdu.de/gratis-heimspeicher-rechner-online/

Flow Requirements:
- Calculators MUST NOT generate individual automated PDF quotes or formal price quotes, as transparent prices are already listed online in `/shop/`.
- Calculator output MUST redirect or pass parameters directly to the consultation page: `https://werdu.de/beratung-anfragen/`.
- On `https://werdu.de/beratung-anfragen/`, the user's calculated parameters (e.g., consumption, PV size, recommended kWh capacity) MUST pre-fill into the lead contact form so the customer can submit their details.
- Calculator 2 (Homepage) and Calculator 3 MUST act as quick previews and seamlessly pass parameters (via URL query parameters or session storage) to Calculator 1 or directly to `https://werdu.de/beratung-anfragen/`.

## 6. LOCAL INSTALLER OPTION
- We do not issue complex custom quotes, but we offer an optional Installer Shipping & Setup Option.
- When selected, the battery is shipped directly to the nearest certified local installer. Upon delivery, the installer handles the physical installation at the customer's house.
- Hourly rates are set by the individual installer — never invent a global setup price.
- UX Integration: Integrate this choice clearly on product pages, checkout (`/kasse/`), and inside the consultation flow (`/beratung-anfragen/`).

## 7. LIGHTHOUSE PERFORMANCE FIXES
Target: FCP < 1.5s, LCP < 2.5s, Mobile PageSpeed >= 87, SEO 100. Eliminate the ~4.4s render-blocking CSS/JS delay.

- Inline critical header/hero CSS in `<head>`. Do not block first paint with Font Awesome `all.min.css`, cart CSS, or non-critical Elementor/theme stylesheets.
- Non-critical CSS: preload / `media="print"` + onload swap, or equivalent deferred load. Non-critical JS: `defer` or `async`.
- Fonts: apply `font-display: swap;` to all `@font-face` rules (theme fonts, Google fonts, Font Awesome).
- Hero / LCP image MUST have `fetchpriority="high"`, `decoding="async"`, explicit `width` and `height`. NEVER `loading="lazy"` on the hero image.
- Prefer system font stack plus swap; avoid render-blocking webfont CSS in the critical path.
- Animate only `transform` and `opacity`. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## 8. RANK MATH SEO
- Custom PHP templates MUST ALWAYS include `wp_head();` inside `<head>` and `wp_footer();` before `</body>`.
- NEVER bypass or strip WordPress core SEO hooks that Rank Math uses for titles, meta descriptions, canonicals, and Open Graph.
- Exactly ONE `<h1>` per page. Subsections follow `<h2>` then `<h3>`.
- Minimum 2200+ words of high-value German content on custom landing templates.
- BLUF: every H2/H3 section starts with a 1–2 sentence direct answer.
- JSON-LD: `FAQPage`, `Product` / `Offer`, `SoftwareApplication` (calculators), `BreadcrumbList` where applicable.
- FAQs: 8–10 in-depth items (not one-liners) plus matching `FAQPage` schema.
- Preserve dynamic WooCommerce / Preis-Manager shortcodes (`do_shortcode('[werdu_preis id="..."]')`). Never hardcode product prices.

## 9. AUTOMATED GIT DEPLOYMENT
After completing requested file modifications, always deploy to staging by running in the repo root:

1. `git add .`
2. `git commit -m "..."` with a concise message describing why the change exists
3. `git push` to the active branch (`origin main` unless another branch is checked out)

This triggers the automatic deployment pipeline to https://test.werdu.de. Do not skip the push after homepage/template/performance work unless the user explicitly forbids git in that turn. Never use `--no-verify`, force-push, or rewrite published history.

