## 11. STRICT CODE & EXECUTION RULES
- NEVER remove existing core functionality without replacement.
- DO NOT invent non-existent file paths or missing functions. Always inspect existing code files first.
- Maintain absolute isolation for calculator scripts (e.g., `#werdu-calc-isolated`) to avoid theme CSS/JS conflicts.
- Ensure all German text produced is grammatically flawless, natural, and highly professional.
- Do not leave unfinished TODO comments in production code.
- NEVER truncate code. Always output complete code files from top to bottom.
- NEVER use placeholder comments such as `// ... rest of code` or `/* TODO */`.

## 12. CSS & LAYOUT BUG PREVENTION
- SKIP-LINK BUG FIX: `a.skip-link, .skip-link, .screen-reader-text:focus { display: none !important; }`
- TITLE GRADIENT: `.gradient-title .highlight-gradient { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #00529b 0%, #ff6600 100%); -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; display: inline-block; }`
- CALCULATOR DIMENSIONS: `max-width: 850px !important; width: 100% !important; margin: 0 auto !important; padding: 35px !important;`
- PRODUCT GRID: `display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr)); gap: 25px; align-items: stretch;`
- PRODUCT CARDS: `display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: space-between; height: 100%;`
- BESTSELLER CARD: `border: 2px solid #ff6600 !important;`
- STANDARD CARD: `border: 1px solid #e2e8f0 !important;`
- CTA BOTTOM ALIGN: `margin-top: auto !important; padding-top: 15px !important; border-top: 1px solid #edf2f7 !important;`
- FAQ accordions: native `<details>` / `<summary>`, not JavaScript toggles.
- Custom templates MUST keep `get_header()` / `get_footer()` (or explicit `wp_head()` / `wp_footer()`).
